## Introduction

The `@johnynek/types` package provides support for encoding and decoding between different data types
in JavaScript.

### Overview

This library supports many of the data types used by Node's built-in objects like [`Buffer`](https://nodejs.org/api/buffer.html),
[`Date`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/Date), [`RegExp`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/JavaScript/Reference/Global_Objects/RegExp),
and others. It also defines some additional types that are commonly used throughout the web stack,
like [`URLSearchParams`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/URLSearchParams).

It does **not** provide support for serializing native types such as [`Blob`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/Blob) or [`FileList`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/API/FileList).
These types need to be treated separately since they are opaque blobs where only their byte content is relevant.
